Chapter: DeskRevCacheTest
  cites Works chapter GopDesk
  cites Works chapter GopReview
  cites Foreword chapter CCE

 The Review pane's store is held in `da-review` between keystrokes instead of
 being re-read on each one. The marker in `gd-facts` is what makes the two
 answers distinguishable: this arm runs with NO disk, so a read of the store
 answers `grv-none` and a fact count of 0, and any non-zero count can only have
 come from the carried record. The third line is that control.

 The second line is the invalidation `grv-cast` depends on. `__record-set`
 stores through the caller's pointer, so a cast that reloads into the record
 the desk loop is holding must be visible through the SAME binding that was
 read a moment earlier; if it were not, the pane would show a verdict the
 store does not have.

Section: Body

  drc-mark : Integer -> GrvData
  drc-mark (n) = GrvData { gd-ok = True, gd-base = 0, gd-facts = n, gd-proposals = [], gd-verdicts = [], gd-sups = [] }

  drc-apps : GrvData -> DeskApps
  drc-apps (d) = DeskApps { da-files = None, da-browser = None, da-scene = None, da-edit = None, da-sheet = None, da-review = Just d }

  drc-say : Text, Boolean -> Text
  drc-say (label) (ok) = label & ": " & (if ok then "PASS" else "FAIL")

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console, Device.Port] Nothing = act
    let apps = drc-apps (drc-mark 4242)
    in act
      d0 <- desk-rev-data apps
      print-line-uni (drc-say "the step reads the carried store" (d0.gd-facts == 4242))
      let keep = __record-set apps "da-review" (Just (drc-mark 777))
      in act
        d1 <- desk-rev-data apps
        print-line-uni (drc-say "a reload is visible through the same record" (d1.gd-facts == 777))
        e0 <- desk-rev-data desk-apps-empty
        print-line-uni (drc-say "with nothing carried the store is read" (e0.gd-facts == 0 & e0.gd-ok == False))
      end
    end
  end
